  "body": "The WebDriver BiDi section defines four events, but the `BluetoothEvent` aggregate lists only two of them:\n\n```cddl\nBluetoothEvent = (\n  bluetooth.RequestDevicePromptUpdated //\n  bluetooth.GattConnectionAttempted\n)\n```\n\n`bluetooth.CharacteristicEventGenerated` and `bluetooth.DescriptorEventGenerated` are fully defined further down, with their parameters, but nothing references them.\n\nClients that generate their BiDi types from the extracted CDDL (the `bluetooth-all.cddl` that w3c/webref publishes) discover events through this aggregate, so those two events are unreachable from the grammar. In Selenium I carry a local override that redefines the aggregate to work around it.\n\nProposed fix:\n\n```cddl\nBluetoothEvent = (\n  bluetooth.RequestDevicePromptUpdated //\n  bluetooth.GattConnectionAttempted //\n  bluetooth.CharacteristicEventGenerated //\n  bluetooth.DescriptorEventGenerated\n)\n```\n\nI would have sent a PR, but GitHub isn't letting me fork this repository for some reason (the fork request returns an HTTP 500).\n",
